// AES (FIPS 197) with the CBC, CTR, and GCM modes (NIST SP 800-38A and 800-38D), in pure Burdin.
//
// This is a straightforward byte-oriented AES. It looks up the S-box by secret-dependent index, so on a CPU with
// data caches it can leak the key to a local attacker who shares the cache (the classic AES cache-timing attack).
// For a secret that matters against that attacker use ChaCha20-Poly1305, which has no table lookups.

use errors.CryptoError
use util.constant_time_eq

